# Implementation Plan - Industrial Schema Isolation Fix

I have identified why the 114MB restore is still failing. Your SQL dump contains hardcoded references to the `public` schema (`CREATE TABLE public.abilities`, etc.). Our system tries to isolate everything in a `staging` schema for safety, but these hardcoded references were overriding our settings and causing permission errors that crashed the database pipe.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Schema Rewriting:** I will implement an industrial-grade stream rewriter. As your 114MB file is being piped to the database, the system will dynamically replace `public.` with `staging.` and filter out dangerous commands like `CREATE EXTENSION` which often cause permission failures.

